1
00:00:06,132 --> 00:00:08,050
The Child of Visayas...

2
00:00:08,134 --> 00:00:10,636
Attorney Benjamin Santos!

3
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:13,013
Ben, it's me! Let me in!

4
00:00:13,097 --> 00:00:14,724
- Ma'am--
- Ben!

5
00:00:14,807 --> 00:00:16,183
- Stop!
- Ben!

6
00:00:16,267 --> 00:00:18,728
<i>Your sister?</i>
<i>You hid that from me for eight years!</i>

7
00:00:18,811 --> 00:00:20,062
<i>What am I supposed to do with that?</i>

8
00:00:20,146 --> 00:00:22,356
I didn't lie. I just didn't say.

9
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:23,691
- <i>No! No!</i>
- <i>What do you want?</i>

10
00:00:23,774 --> 00:00:26,652
<i>They say that I'm crazy.</i>
<i>That my screws are loose.</i>

11
00:00:26,736 --> 00:00:29,488
- <i>She could end up killing you.</i>
- Ma!

12
00:00:29,572 --> 00:00:30,990
If that time comes,

13
00:00:31,073 --> 00:00:34,368
it's better to have a gun than a knife.

14
00:00:34,452 --> 00:00:37,079
<i>I just really need to speak with her.</i>

15
00:00:37,163 --> 00:00:40,458
I have something important to tell her.

16
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:42,042
Ben killed my husband.
Ben killed my husband.

17
00:00:42,126 --> 00:00:43,419
Did you see it?

18
00:00:43,502 --> 00:00:45,796
No. But I know he did it.

19
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:03,564
<i>You'll love this.</i>
<i>I know something about you.</i>

20
00:01:03,647 --> 00:01:04,940
<i>No, don't.</i>

21
00:01:05,024 --> 00:01:06,567
<i>I remember every single story</i>
<i>Gingging told me.</i>

22
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:10,863
- Don't! Don't say it!
<i>- About how you killed your father.</i>

23
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:13,282
<i>- Ten million. So we can start over.</i>

24
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:14,867
<i>- Right, Regina?</i>
- <i>Regina, please.</i>

25
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:16,243
<i>Ten million.</i>

26
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:23,991
Ben?

27
00:05:30,414 --> 00:05:31,582
Ben...

28
00:05:43,761 --> 00:05:44,595
Ben?

29
00:05:51,185 --> 00:05:52,311
Ben?

30
00:05:54,313 --> 00:05:55,355
Ben?

31
00:07:15,352 --> 00:07:16,436
Ben!

32
00:07:18,230 --> 00:07:19,565
Where is she?

33
00:07:20,774 --> 00:07:22,860
- Who was that?
- The woman at the gate?

34
00:07:23,569 --> 00:07:25,821
- I don't know. I don't know.
- Who was that?

35
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:28,115
- I almost ran over her.
- What?

36
00:07:29,074 --> 00:07:31,660
Who was that, Nanny?
What did she look like?

37
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:35,581
She had fair skin.
A pretty face, petite body.

38
00:07:35,998 --> 00:07:39,501
She said she had
something important to tell you.

39
00:07:39,585 --> 00:07:40,669
Who was that?

40
00:07:40,752 --> 00:07:42,963
- She didn't give her name?
- No, sir.

41
00:07:43,046 --> 00:07:46,592
I don't know. Maybe she's Beth's friend.
She must've sent her here.

42
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:49,511
I don't know.

43
00:07:51,054 --> 00:07:52,890
Do not let anyone in.

44
00:07:52,973 --> 00:07:54,558
- Make sure of it.
- That's right.

45
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:56,977
- Good thing she left.
- Stay alert.

46
00:07:57,686 --> 00:07:59,271
Did she say anything to you, Nanny?

47
00:08:01,106 --> 00:08:02,232
Ging?

48
00:08:04,151 --> 00:08:05,736
Did you drink your medicine?

49
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:15,662
That looks great.

50
00:08:20,876 --> 00:08:22,377
I didn't catch the balloon.

51
00:08:24,213 --> 00:08:25,839
It slipped out of my hand.

52
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:29,051
So it flew away.

53
00:08:33,222 --> 00:08:34,806
It's free now.

54
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:40,270
It isn't free...

55
00:08:41,688 --> 00:08:42,898
it's alone.

56
00:08:42,981 --> 00:08:45,400


57
00:08:45,484 --> 00:08:46,902
There's a difference.

58
00:08:57,746 --> 00:08:58,789
Ging?

59
00:09:00,666 --> 00:09:02,668
Get better soon, okay?

60
00:09:06,088 --> 00:09:08,924
So you can live with us.

61
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:12,344
We can live happily with Ana.

62
00:09:15,472 --> 00:09:17,891
Why should I believe you?

63
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,063
You never tell the truth.

64
00:09:23,855 --> 00:09:26,024
You're a big liar.

65
00:09:27,776 --> 00:09:30,112
I know you don't love me.

66
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:40,998
Thanks.

67
00:09:51,508 --> 00:09:53,260
Mm.

68
00:10:21,038 --> 00:10:22,164
Ging.

69
00:10:26,168 --> 00:10:27,502
I love you.

70
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:30,505
I love you so much.

71
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:34,092
What makes you think I don't?

72
00:10:35,302 --> 00:10:36,303
Hmm?

73
00:10:38,722 --> 00:10:41,558
Then why are you sending me away
to a facility?

74
00:10:43,769 --> 00:10:46,438
And you tie me up.

75
00:10:46,521 --> 00:10:49,441
You keep me locked away and hidden.

76
00:10:51,443 --> 00:10:56,031
Ging, you're sick, remember?

77
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:59,117
This is what's best for you.

78
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:03,246
How is this supposed to be
what's best for me?

79
00:11:03,872 --> 00:11:05,374
Where are you?

80
00:11:06,208 --> 00:11:07,459
Huh?

81
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:10,128
You're in this fancy house.

82
00:11:10,212 --> 00:11:12,339
Living a good life

83
00:11:12,422 --> 00:11:14,758
with your beautiful wife.

84
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:16,134
And what about me?

85
00:11:17,803 --> 00:11:22,516
Mara's the one
who takes care of me, not you.

86
00:11:22,599 --> 00:11:24,518
I love you, Ging.

87
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:26,853
Mara's here because of me.

88
00:11:27,437 --> 00:11:30,023
I pay her to take care of you.

89
00:11:30,107 --> 00:11:32,109
You should be taking care of me.

90
00:11:32,984 --> 00:11:35,570
Ging.

91
00:11:37,656 --> 00:11:40,158
Ging, you ran away, remember?

92
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:45,831
I had to work hard
and build a life for myself.

93
00:11:46,957 --> 00:11:48,542
So when we'd meet again--

94
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:50,836
You could send me to a mental facility?

95
00:11:50,919 --> 00:11:52,003
Ging...

96
00:11:52,629 --> 00:11:53,797
Ging.

97
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:56,675
I just want you to get better.

98
00:11:56,758 --> 00:12:00,053
Nobody loves me.

99
00:12:01,096 --> 00:12:03,515
They've all left me.

100
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:07,227
Ging.

101
00:12:07,310 --> 00:12:09,521
You've all left me!

102
00:12:10,105 --> 00:12:12,941
Ging. I'm still here.

103
00:12:13,316 --> 00:12:15,152
I love you.

104
00:12:16,153 --> 00:12:18,238
I am your brother.

105
00:12:18,321 --> 00:12:20,407
Yes, you're my brother.

106
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,619
So you have no choice but to love me.

107
00:12:27,205 --> 00:12:30,792
If I wasn't your sister,
you would've killed me a long time ago.

108
00:12:34,421 --> 00:12:36,840
You only love one person.

109
00:12:40,427 --> 00:12:42,053
You only love yourself.

110
00:12:57,777 --> 00:13:00,572
A compound? What's inside it?

111
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:01,823
I don't know.

112
00:13:01,907 --> 00:13:06,036
The woman at the store doesn't know
what's inside either.

113
00:13:06,119 --> 00:13:08,955
<i>I just saw a guy with a gun.</i>

114
00:13:09,039 --> 00:13:12,834
<i>Are you sure, Bridge?</i>
<i>What if Angel's not there?</i>

115
00:13:12,918 --> 00:13:17,672
<i>I showed the woman</i>
<i>Angel's picture. She said...</i>

116
00:13:17,756 --> 00:13:20,008
Oh, yes. The girl with the fair skin!

117
00:13:20,467 --> 00:13:23,678
She sent money from here.

118
00:13:23,762 --> 00:13:27,098
If I'm not mistaken,
she lives in the Abismo Compound.

119
00:13:28,183 --> 00:13:29,768
<i>She said the girl had fair skin!</i>

120
00:13:29,851 --> 00:13:34,189
Angel has fair skin. It has to be her!

121
00:13:35,774 --> 00:13:37,776
What if we report it to the police?

122
00:13:37,859 --> 00:13:41,655
Remember? Rona said
no one reports the cops.

123
00:13:41,738 --> 00:13:43,657
But we need help.

124
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:46,618
Who knows what happened to Angel.

125
00:13:53,458 --> 00:13:56,127
It's nice to walk around here.

126
00:13:56,795 --> 00:13:59,047
Thank you for joining me.

127
00:13:59,130 --> 00:14:01,800
A change of scenery will do you good.

128
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:08,265
Do you like your dress?

129
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,562
Okay.

130
00:14:13,645 --> 00:14:18,024
After the fundraiser
and my friend's wedding,

131
00:14:18,108 --> 00:14:19,609
I'll make you another one.

132
00:14:19,693 --> 00:14:20,860
It really suits you.

133
00:14:21,945 --> 00:14:24,614
What is a fundraiser?

134
00:14:25,365 --> 00:14:27,867
It's like a... party.

135
00:14:27,951 --> 00:14:33,290
They'll showcase my designs,
and people will come to buy them.

136
00:14:33,373 --> 00:14:38,378
The money we'll raise will be donated
to a charitable organization.

137
00:14:38,461 --> 00:14:43,216
Like a hospital or orphanage.

138
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:46,803
You're going to give your clothes away
for free?

139
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:50,640
Mm-hmm. To help the poor.

140
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:53,810
You're such a good person.

141
00:14:54,394 --> 00:14:56,563
You care for those in need.

142
00:14:57,814 --> 00:14:59,316
Like me.

143
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:03,903
My brother and I
used to rely on food drives.

144
00:15:04,362 --> 00:15:05,822
Did you know that?

145
00:15:06,406 --> 00:15:08,825
Yes.

146
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:10,994
You know, he's really nice.

147
00:15:12,037 --> 00:15:15,123
He'd always protect me from bullies.

148
00:15:16,291 --> 00:15:19,127
There used to be bad kids
in our neighborhood.

149
00:15:21,713 --> 00:15:22,964
And also from...

150
00:15:24,799 --> 00:15:26,051
Papa.

151
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:29,679
He'd always protect me from Papa.

152
00:15:31,139 --> 00:15:33,391
One time, when Papa touched me,

153
00:15:33,975 --> 00:15:36,311
he said, "Stop!

154
00:15:36,686 --> 00:15:38,938
No! Don't do that to Ging!"

155
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:44,444
How would he touch you?

156
00:15:50,575 --> 00:15:51,743
Like this.

157
00:15:54,663 --> 00:15:55,830
Right here.

158
00:15:58,708 --> 00:15:59,876
Sometimes...

159
00:16:03,797 --> 00:16:06,299
I don't know. I don't remember.

160
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:10,220
I'd just feel bad for Ben.

161
00:16:10,804 --> 00:16:12,889
He'd always get beaten up.

162
00:16:13,932 --> 00:16:15,350
But he's a nice kid.

163
00:16:18,228 --> 00:16:20,563
He's nice to me too, Regina.

164
00:16:21,231 --> 00:16:24,234
He helps a lot of people in Vallente.

165
00:16:25,819 --> 00:16:27,821
He's loved by many.

166
00:16:31,658 --> 00:16:34,411
Sure. He's a nice guy.

167
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:37,747
But he's done terrible things too.

168
00:16:40,417 --> 00:16:42,001
What do you mean?

169
00:16:42,877 --> 00:16:45,880
Have I told you
it's not just Joel he'd killed?

170
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:48,925
He killed Papa too.

171
00:16:49,008 --> 00:16:50,927
I saw it with my own eyes.

172
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,471
That's not a good joke, Regina.

173
00:16:54,514 --> 00:16:56,933
Do I look like I'm joking?

174
00:16:59,853 --> 00:17:03,606
Do you really think
you know everything about him?

175
00:17:05,859 --> 00:17:07,694
He didn't even go to school.

176
00:17:08,695 --> 00:17:10,447
He's not a real lawyer.

177
00:17:11,489 --> 00:17:13,158
He's such a fraud.

178
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,369
Ben isn't a real lawyer?

179
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:21,124
I really like this dress.

180
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:24,419
It suits my necklace.

181
00:17:24,502 --> 00:17:26,504
Joel gave this to me.

182
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:30,300
Yes, it's pretty.

183
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:32,343
Come on, Regina. Let's go home.

184
00:17:32,969 --> 00:17:34,053
Joel?

185
00:17:34,846 --> 00:17:36,598
- Joel!
- Regina!

186
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:39,184
Joel!

187
00:17:39,934 --> 00:17:40,935
Regina.

188
00:17:43,271 --> 00:17:44,522
You're not him.

189
00:17:47,150 --> 00:17:48,735
- Let's go.
- It's not him.

190
00:17:50,528 --> 00:17:51,613
Come on.

191
00:17:53,615 --> 00:17:55,784
I know, I know!

192
00:17:56,242 --> 00:17:58,453
<i>Let's not argue about this.</i>

193
00:17:59,454 --> 00:18:01,623
You shouldn't have let her out.

194
00:18:02,165 --> 00:18:04,167
<i>I thought it would be okay, Ben.</i>

195
00:18:04,584 --> 00:18:07,003
<i>We had security with us.</i>

196
00:18:07,545 --> 00:18:09,297
Anyway, I'm on my way home. Okay?

197
00:18:26,981 --> 00:18:30,610
We've also reported it to the police,
but they told us

198
00:18:30,693 --> 00:18:33,279
we didn't have enough evidence
to make a case.

199
00:18:34,072 --> 00:18:35,907
What did you expect?

200
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:38,243
Eric has connections
within the police force.

201
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:41,412
But wait, did you go alone?

202
00:18:41,496 --> 00:18:42,914
That's too dangerous.

203
00:18:43,414 --> 00:18:45,500
I need to know the truth.

204
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,544
My God, Bridgette.

205
00:18:47,627 --> 00:18:49,295
I can't do that kind of thing.

206
00:18:49,379 --> 00:18:50,797
It's not that.

207
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:55,051
But do you know someone

208
00:18:55,134 --> 00:19:00,807
who can help us get Angel
out of that goddamn compound?

209
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:09,399
Here. Call that number.

210
00:19:09,899 --> 00:19:12,652
Who is this? How can they help me?

211
00:19:13,403 --> 00:19:15,738
Just call them and say you know me.

212
00:19:18,741 --> 00:19:23,830
Oh, whoever that is,
I really hope they can help Angel.

213
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:30,628
Excuse me, one gin tonic, please.

214
00:19:42,098 --> 00:19:44,434
Ow! Watch it.

215
00:19:45,268 --> 00:19:46,436
Sorry, sorry.

216
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:47,729
Isn't that the physical therapist?

217
00:19:47,812 --> 00:19:49,647
The one who worked for the Saguils?

218
00:19:50,064 --> 00:19:53,693
You mean, the girl who tried
stealing Ana Santos's husband?

219
00:19:53,776 --> 00:19:54,861
Yeah.

220
00:19:56,946 --> 00:19:58,823
Are you guys talking about me?

221
00:19:58,907 --> 00:20:00,658
Yeah, we'd like to know how you do it.

222
00:20:00,742 --> 00:20:02,577
First, be a skank.

223
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:06,247
Then, pretend to be a PT
to get close to married men.

224
00:20:06,331 --> 00:20:07,415
What did you say?

225
00:20:07,498 --> 00:20:08,917
- You've got a lot of nerve.
- Hey!

226
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:12,754
- What did you do?
- Leave me alone, you two.

227
00:20:12,837 --> 00:20:14,088
Oh, did I offend you?

228
00:20:14,172 --> 00:20:17,425
- You've got some guts, don't you?
- Ow! Let me go! Ow!

229
00:20:17,508 --> 00:20:19,218
You deserve it, whore!

230
00:20:19,302 --> 00:20:20,887
- Take this!
- Stop! Hey!

231
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:24,015
- Take that!
- Stop!

232
00:20:24,098 --> 00:20:26,559
You think you're tough, huh?

233
00:20:26,643 --> 00:20:27,894
- You're just a skank!
- You deserve that!

234
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:30,271
If I were you, I'd leave this place!

235
00:20:30,355 --> 00:20:32,398
<i> Get out, skank!</i>

236
00:20:32,482 --> 00:20:33,650
<i> Stop!</i>

237
00:20:57,507 --> 00:20:58,841
Hello?

238
00:20:58,925 --> 00:21:01,177
You finally remembered to call!

239
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,346
I was wondering how you've been.

240
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:08,893
Betchay?

241
00:21:11,437 --> 00:21:13,940
What happened to you?

242
00:21:15,566 --> 00:21:16,776
At the bar...

243
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:22,031
I got...

244
00:21:22,115 --> 00:21:23,616
I got beaten up.

245
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:25,326
<i>You got into a fight?</i>

246
00:21:25,410 --> 00:21:28,496
You can't just get wasted.
You're an outsider!

247
00:21:36,546 --> 00:21:38,381
Diane, what did I do wrong?

248
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:45,263
Why is this so hard for me?

249
00:21:47,974 --> 00:21:49,892
All I did was love a guy.

250
00:21:51,227 --> 00:21:53,312
You loved a married man.

251
00:21:53,688 --> 00:21:54,856
<i>But...</i>

252
00:21:56,107 --> 00:21:57,942
<i>that's how love is, right?</i>

253
00:21:58,026 --> 00:21:59,527
<i>You can't help it.</i>

254
00:22:01,612 --> 00:22:04,198
You just feel it.

255
00:22:05,992 --> 00:22:07,660
You just... love.

256
00:22:10,246 --> 00:22:12,081
Betchay, the real question is...

257
00:22:12,165 --> 00:22:14,876
are you sure that's love?

258
00:22:14,959 --> 00:22:17,378
<i>I wouldn't be crazy over Ben like this...</i>

259
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:20,465
if it wasn't love.

260
00:22:23,885 --> 00:22:24,969
<i>Why?</i>

261
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:29,057
<i>Do you think love is the only thing</i>
<i>that could drive a person mad?</i>

262
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:33,352
What... what do you mean?

263
00:22:34,479 --> 00:22:37,065
Sometimes, loneliness is far worse.

264
00:22:39,108 --> 00:22:40,443
<i>Being alone...</i>

265
00:22:42,403 --> 00:22:44,655
<i>takes a lot out of you.</i>

266
00:22:47,533 --> 00:22:51,370
<i>So, if you ask me again, Beth,</i>

267
00:22:52,455 --> 00:22:54,791
if we can choose the people we love...

268
00:22:55,249 --> 00:22:56,417
yes, we can.

269
00:22:56,876 --> 00:22:58,461
You can choose.

270
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:03,800
And you can choose the people
who actually love you back.

271
00:23:07,136 --> 00:23:08,763
Your family.

272
00:23:12,934 --> 00:23:14,936
Yourself.

273
00:23:17,522 --> 00:23:19,607
<i>Come home, Beth, please?</i>

274
00:23:20,525 --> 00:23:22,777
We will all be waiting for you here.

275
00:23:45,758 --> 00:23:47,677
<i>He didn't even go to school.</i>

276
00:23:48,719 --> 00:23:50,638
<i>He's not a real lawyer.</i>

277
00:24:15,788 --> 00:24:16,622
Hey.

278
00:24:18,624 --> 00:24:20,209
Oh. Hey, stranger.

279
00:24:20,293 --> 00:24:21,544
How are you?

280
00:24:24,255 --> 00:24:25,339
Good.

281
00:25:13,012 --> 00:25:14,597
No!

282
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:16,557
- I don't want to go, Ben!
- It's safe there.

283
00:25:16,641 --> 00:25:18,392
- People are nice.
- What's going on?

284
00:25:18,476 --> 00:25:20,561
What's happening? Wait!

285
00:25:20,645 --> 00:25:21,896
Let her go!

286
00:25:21,979 --> 00:25:24,357
- I don't want to go!
- Let her go! Let her go!

287
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:27,818
- Stop hurting her!
- I don't want to go!

288
00:25:27,902 --> 00:25:31,239
Ben, she's your sister!
You shouldn't do this to her!

289
00:25:31,322 --> 00:25:33,574
- I know that, Ana.
- She doesn't wanna go!

290
00:25:33,658 --> 00:25:35,493
But she's unstable.

291
00:25:35,576 --> 00:25:38,329
She's unstable. She has to go.

292
00:25:38,412 --> 00:25:41,707
She has to go. Trust me, please.
Trust me, I know what I'm doing.

293
00:25:41,791 --> 00:25:44,085
- Ging...
- No, please, Ben!

294
00:25:44,168 --> 00:25:46,671
I'll come back for you, okay?

295
00:25:46,754 --> 00:25:47,964
We're going to fix this.

296
00:25:48,047 --> 00:25:50,883
It won't take long.
Everyone there is nice.

297
00:25:50,967 --> 00:25:52,802
I promise, I won't leave you alone.

298
00:25:53,344 --> 00:25:54,845
- I don't want to!
- I won't leave you alone.

299
00:25:54,929 --> 00:25:57,682
Ana, I don't want to go.

300
00:25:57,765 --> 00:25:59,684
I don't want to!

301
00:25:59,767 --> 00:26:02,019
Ben, I don't want to go!

302
00:26:02,103 --> 00:26:04,814
I really don't want to!

303
00:26:04,897 --> 00:26:07,066
- Don't make me go!
- I won't leave you alone.

304
00:26:07,149 --> 00:26:08,359
Please...

305
00:26:08,442 --> 00:26:11,320
I don't want to go there!

306
00:26:11,404 --> 00:26:13,531
Don't make them take me, please.

307
00:26:13,614 --> 00:26:16,200
I don't want to go!

308
00:26:17,159 --> 00:26:21,580
I don't want to go there!

309
00:26:21,664 --> 00:26:24,083
Please, Ben.

310
00:26:24,166 --> 00:26:25,626
I'll come back for you.

311
00:26:25,710 --> 00:26:27,753
I promise, I'll come back for you.

312
00:26:27,837 --> 00:26:29,005
Okay?

313
00:26:30,256 --> 00:26:33,342
Wait for me, okay? Just be good.

314
00:26:33,426 --> 00:26:34,593
Go on now.

315
00:26:35,845 --> 00:26:38,681
Come on now. It's for your own good.

316
00:26:38,764 --> 00:26:41,100
You'll be fine over there.

317
00:26:41,642 --> 00:26:43,394
I got this. Thank you.

318
00:27:05,166 --> 00:27:07,084
You did the right thing.

319
00:27:07,585 --> 00:27:08,753
I should know.

320
00:27:09,670 --> 00:27:12,590
I also get treated for my mental health.

321
00:27:13,299 --> 00:27:16,302
That's all you want for your sister.

322
00:27:19,221 --> 00:27:22,850
I don't know,
but why do I feel like...

323
00:27:23,309 --> 00:27:25,144
Ana doesn't like what I did?

324
00:27:25,644 --> 00:27:28,898
Not everything is right feels right.

325
00:27:29,690 --> 00:27:32,610
And not everything that feels wrong
is wrong.

326
00:27:34,153 --> 00:27:37,823
Maybe Ana is concerned about your sister

327
00:27:38,491 --> 00:27:41,077
because she reminds her of her brother.

328
00:27:42,286 --> 00:27:44,622
She wants to help Regina because...

329
00:27:45,289 --> 00:27:47,625
she couldn't help her brother before.

330
00:27:53,130 --> 00:27:56,467
Just try to understand.

331
00:27:56,842 --> 00:27:59,011
She's been through so much.

332
00:28:00,971 --> 00:28:02,139
Actually...

333
00:28:03,265 --> 00:28:06,018
there's one more thing
I wanted to discuss with you,

334
00:28:06,102 --> 00:28:07,353
if that's okay.

335
00:28:10,356 --> 00:28:11,941
The Bais house.

336
00:28:14,318 --> 00:28:16,570
I'd like to buy the Bais house.

337
00:28:17,321 --> 00:28:19,573
Of course,
at the price that you like.

338
00:28:22,618 --> 00:28:24,703
It's a gift for my wife.

339
00:28:25,788 --> 00:28:27,123
Of course.

340
00:28:27,873 --> 00:28:29,625
If that's what you want.

341
00:28:30,292 --> 00:28:33,045
I'm sure Ana would love that too.

342
00:28:37,425 --> 00:28:39,260
That's all I want.

343
00:28:40,636 --> 00:28:42,054
You know, Ben...

344
00:28:42,138 --> 00:28:44,140
sometimes I wonder.

345
00:28:44,849 --> 00:28:47,351
What would happen to my daughter
without you?

346
00:29:02,867 --> 00:29:04,285
<i>He's a nice guy.</i>

347
00:29:05,202 --> 00:29:07,621
<i>But he's done terrible things too.</i>

348
00:29:08,914 --> 00:29:13,419
<i>Do you really think</i>
<i>you know everything about him?</i>

349
00:29:14,211 --> 00:29:16,213
<i>He's not a real lawyer.</i>

350
00:29:16,964 --> 00:29:18,466
<i>He's such a fraud.</i>

351
00:29:19,383 --> 00:29:22,219
Have I told you
it's not just Joel he'd killed?

352
00:29:23,304 --> 00:29:26,974
He killed Papa too.
I saw it with my own eyes.

353
00:31:19,670 --> 00:31:22,089
Ana! Ana!

354
00:31:23,507 --> 00:31:24,592
Ana!

355
00:31:59,376 --> 00:32:01,128
What are you doing here?

356
00:32:05,257 --> 00:32:07,259
I'm ready to tell the whole truth.

357
00:32:21,357 --> 00:32:22,441
Not here.

358
00:32:26,028 --> 00:32:30,366
I asked you before,
and you said you didn't know Ben.

359
00:32:30,449 --> 00:32:33,285
But now you're telling me
you know something about him.

360
00:32:34,370 --> 00:32:36,455
Why should I believe you?

361
00:32:37,998 --> 00:32:41,418
I only said that because I promised Ben.

362
00:32:43,754 --> 00:32:45,339
But I'm not his mistress.

363
00:32:46,548 --> 00:32:48,217
I'm his sister's nurse.

364
00:32:48,759 --> 00:32:50,678
And the house you went to...

365
00:32:51,053 --> 00:32:53,138
that's where your husband was hiding us.

366
00:32:54,765 --> 00:32:57,434
Ben said that was the first time
he saw his sister again.

367
00:32:57,518 --> 00:32:58,769
That's not true.

368
00:32:59,520 --> 00:33:01,939
He's hiding a lot from you.

369
00:33:03,273 --> 00:33:04,692
Like this.

370
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:08,320
Look at it.

371
00:33:08,612 --> 00:33:10,614
This is one of the copies
that slipped past Ben

372
00:33:10,698 --> 00:33:12,199
and Attorney De Castro.

373
00:33:12,741 --> 00:33:14,326
Check this.

374
00:33:18,622 --> 00:33:21,125
Yes, Benjamin Santos is a common name.

375
00:33:21,208 --> 00:33:22,793
But if he really graduated there,

376
00:33:22,876 --> 00:33:25,295
then there should be two of them
in the yearbook.

377
00:33:28,215 --> 00:33:29,466
No, no.

378
00:33:29,550 --> 00:33:33,762
I called the university,
and they said Ben did graduate there.

379
00:33:33,846 --> 00:33:35,806
Maybe he just didn't sign up for this.

380
00:33:36,181 --> 00:33:38,434
This is the IBP number
that he's been using.

381
00:33:39,059 --> 00:33:41,895
This is the one. Right?

382
00:33:43,605 --> 00:33:46,191
I traced the registered owner.

383
00:33:46,692 --> 00:33:48,527
It turned out to be a different Ben.

384
00:33:50,404 --> 00:33:54,158
It's the one, right?
Attorney Ben's IBP number?

385
00:33:55,284 --> 00:33:56,702
Indeed, this IBP number is registered

386
00:33:56,785 --> 00:33:58,537
to Attorney Benjamin Santos.

387
00:34:00,205 --> 00:34:02,040
But why are you searching for him?

388
00:34:03,125 --> 00:34:05,169
He has long been deceased.

389
00:34:08,547 --> 00:34:09,882
W-What?

390
00:34:09,965 --> 00:34:11,467
For almost ten years now.

391
00:34:12,134 --> 00:34:13,719
He's been dead for years.

392
00:34:16,346 --> 00:34:19,266
Ben is a good person. He's a good man.

393
00:34:19,349 --> 00:34:21,852
- He's good...
- He's good at lying!

394
00:34:22,436 --> 00:34:25,272
You married a fraud, Ana!

395
00:34:28,942 --> 00:34:30,944
Who told you about this?

396
00:34:31,028 --> 00:34:32,196
Regina?

397
00:34:32,654 --> 00:34:35,157
You know she's sick, right?

398
00:34:36,450 --> 00:34:39,203
I came face-to-face
with someone from Ben's past.

399
00:34:42,206 --> 00:34:45,876
My father worked at your law firm
for many years.

400
00:34:49,379 --> 00:34:52,382
And still, I never received any help.

401
00:34:55,385 --> 00:34:58,889
What... would you like to know?

402
00:34:58,972 --> 00:35:02,226
I just want to know if you can help me.

403
00:35:02,684 --> 00:35:03,936
Of course.

404
00:35:04,645 --> 00:35:06,730
Sure. I'll help you.

405
00:35:07,481 --> 00:35:09,983
If it's what will cause Ben's downfall.

406
00:35:13,695 --> 00:35:15,280
That bastard Ben...

407
00:35:16,448 --> 00:35:19,284
he hogged all the luck in the world.

408
00:35:20,369 --> 00:35:22,454
While the rest of us are struggling,

409
00:35:23,497 --> 00:35:26,166
still-- still sunken deep here
at the bottom.

410
00:35:29,670 --> 00:35:31,672
Who killed my father?

411
00:35:34,967 --> 00:35:36,218
Was it Ben?

412
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:42,558
It wasn't Ben.

413
00:35:44,560 --> 00:35:45,894
It was De Castro.

414
00:35:49,106 --> 00:35:51,775
De Castro killed your father.

415
00:35:54,862 --> 00:35:58,365
De Castro fought with another lawyer
from a different firm.

416
00:35:59,616 --> 00:36:01,869
De Castro shot him.

417
00:36:02,828 --> 00:36:04,997
How very unfortunate...

418
00:36:06,874 --> 00:36:09,459
that your father witnessed it all.

419
00:36:13,839 --> 00:36:15,841
They killed my father...

420
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:18,760
to shut him up?

421
00:36:18,844 --> 00:36:21,680
It was Ben who made it seem like

422
00:36:21,763 --> 00:36:26,101
your father was a drug addict
and committed suicide.

423
00:36:26,518 --> 00:36:31,356
He was the one who covered up everything
to avoid anything from coming out.

424
00:36:33,901 --> 00:36:36,069
<i>When I found out the truth...</i>

425
00:36:39,656 --> 00:36:42,492
I was so infuriated
that I wanted to take revenge.

426
00:36:45,454 --> 00:36:48,707
I want justice for my father.

427
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:54,838
Sue De Castro.

428
00:36:55,339 --> 00:36:56,924
Ask for Brian's help

429
00:36:57,007 --> 00:36:59,176
if he's really the one
who knows everything.

430
00:36:59,259 --> 00:37:01,178
Brian is gone, Ana.

431
00:37:02,304 --> 00:37:04,973
After that day,
I never saw him again.

432
00:37:05,057 --> 00:37:06,642
He's gone.

433
00:37:09,561 --> 00:37:11,480
No, I just saw Brian.

434
00:37:11,563 --> 00:37:13,357
He stopped by our house.

435
00:37:13,440 --> 00:37:15,859
- He's going through something.
- No, he's not.

436
00:37:16,276 --> 00:37:18,278
Ben's money is all he's after.

437
00:37:25,661 --> 00:37:29,331
Ana, with how long
I've been looking after Regina,

438
00:37:31,166 --> 00:37:35,003
she's told me a lot about the things
Ben does to other people.

439
00:37:40,550 --> 00:37:42,970
About what he did to Joel.

440
00:37:45,180 --> 00:37:46,515
To their father.

441
00:37:52,604 --> 00:37:54,606
You believe her?

442
00:37:59,861 --> 00:38:03,281
Even if Regina has
an intellectual disability, in here...

443
00:38:04,199 --> 00:38:05,867
in here, she's genuine.

444
00:38:11,581 --> 00:38:15,168
It's too late to do anything
about my father's case now.

445
00:38:15,544 --> 00:38:16,962
But you...

446
00:38:19,589 --> 00:38:22,175
<i>you can still save yourself.</i>

447
00:39:04,217 --> 00:39:06,303
- Good morning.
- Good morning, sir.

448
00:39:07,304 --> 00:39:09,139
Why is there
just one set? Did Ana eat already?

449
00:39:09,765 --> 00:39:11,349
She already left, sir.

450
00:39:13,643 --> 00:39:14,728
Huh?

451
00:39:14,811 --> 00:39:17,481
Isn't today Ma'am Katrina's wedding day?

452
00:39:18,440 --> 00:39:22,444
She even brought her dress with her.
She might have gone there already.

453
00:39:24,029 --> 00:39:26,031
She didn't mention anything to me
about that.

454
00:39:26,573 --> 00:39:28,241
I was taken by surprise as well.

455
00:39:28,325 --> 00:39:31,995
But it's Ma'am Katrina's wedding,
so I didn't think too much of it.

456
00:40:34,724 --> 00:40:35,976
Shit.

457
00:41:02,752 --> 00:41:04,379

You don't have to pick me up.

458
00:41:04,462 --> 00:41:07,132
I'll take a taxi
when I get to the airport.

459
00:41:07,966 --> 00:41:11,469
<i>You're bringing all of that?</i>
<i>Aren't you going back there?</i>

460
00:41:12,762 --> 00:41:16,683
Beth, tell us what's wrong.

461
00:41:16,766 --> 00:41:19,436
Nothing. I just really wanted to go home.

462
00:41:19,853 --> 00:41:21,104
Just last time,

463
00:41:21,188 --> 00:41:23,773
we're talking about
how lucky you are in Vallente.

464
00:41:23,857 --> 00:41:25,692
Right? Now, all of a sudden,
you're coming home.

465
00:41:26,234 --> 00:41:28,153
Because of you.

466
00:41:28,528 --> 00:41:31,198
You two are the reason I want to go home.

467
00:41:32,324 --> 00:41:33,742
<i>Really?</i>

468
00:41:34,326 --> 00:41:36,161
You keep thinking of weird things.

469
00:41:36,536 --> 00:41:39,789
I miss you.
That's why I'm going home. That's it.

470
00:41:41,458 --> 00:41:45,462
<i>Okay. If that's the case,</i>
<i>then bring us lots of souvenirs.</i>

471
00:41:45,545 --> 00:41:48,715
<i>Bring home some sweet food too.</i>
<i>Those are yummy!</i>

472
00:41:48,798 --> 00:41:51,384
<i>And when you get here, let's eat out!</i>

473
00:41:51,468 --> 00:41:52,552
- Sure!
<i>- My favorite place!</i>

474
00:41:52,636 --> 00:41:55,055
You keep thinking of food!
It's all just food with you!

475
00:41:55,138 --> 00:41:56,473
- 'Cause I'm hungry--
- Beth, I like seafood.

476
00:41:56,556 --> 00:41:59,559
Mine's seafood, okay?
I want lots of crabs!

477
00:41:59,643 --> 00:42:01,394
- <i>Okay. See you, Beth!</i>
- <i>See you, Beth!</i>

478
00:42:01,478 --> 00:42:02,979
<i>- Take care, okay?</i>
- <i>Take care.</i>

479
00:42:21,289 --> 00:42:24,209
Get away from me, you lunatic!

480
00:42:24,292 --> 00:42:27,212
Nurse,
she's having an episode!

481
00:42:27,295 --> 00:42:28,338
Don't bother me!

482
00:42:28,421 --> 00:42:29,798
- I'll do whatever I want!
- Nurse Chloe,

483
00:42:29,881 --> 00:42:31,466
- you have to ask for help.
- She's so nosy.

484
00:42:31,549 --> 00:42:33,134
She's so nosy!

485
00:43:20,140 --> 00:43:21,391
<i>Ben.</i>

486
00:43:22,309 --> 00:43:23,810
Fuck you, Mara.

487
00:43:24,894 --> 00:43:26,563
I know everything, Ben.

488
00:43:27,272 --> 00:43:28,773
You bastards.

489
00:43:30,734 --> 00:43:33,069
Even though De Castro killed my dad,

490
00:43:33,153 --> 00:43:36,573
you're the reason why there's still
no justice for his death!

491
00:43:37,198 --> 00:43:39,784
That's why I'll ruin both of your lives.

492
00:43:40,160 --> 00:43:41,661
I just started with you.

493
00:43:45,332 --> 00:43:48,168
Well, I can't blame you for being stupid.

494
00:43:52,714 --> 00:43:54,049
You knew.

495
00:43:54,632 --> 00:43:55,717
Obviously.

496
00:43:56,593 --> 00:43:58,345
You think I didn't know?

497
00:43:59,137 --> 00:44:01,806
If you didn't want anything,
would you put up with my sister?

498
00:44:03,892 --> 00:44:07,395
Well, life is like that.
We're all just using each other.

499
00:44:10,315 --> 00:44:13,068
I just targeted Regina
because I needed to know

500
00:44:13,151 --> 00:44:15,153
what really happened to my father.

501
00:44:16,654 --> 00:44:19,407
But I felt nothing for her but sympathy.

502
00:44:22,327 --> 00:44:23,745
I genuinely treated her

503
00:44:23,828 --> 00:44:28,208
like my real family,
which she never felt from you.

504
00:44:29,751 --> 00:44:31,336
Damn you.

505
00:44:31,878 --> 00:44:35,507
Your sympathies are fake, Mara.

506
00:44:35,590 --> 00:44:39,594
You brainwashed my sister
so that she'd be angry with me.

507
00:44:40,095 --> 00:44:41,262
Right?

508
00:44:41,930 --> 00:44:44,933
- Right?
<i>- Say whatever you want to say, Ben.</i>

509
00:44:45,850 --> 00:44:48,353
<i>Because the life you know ends here.</i>

510
00:44:48,978 --> 00:44:50,563
The life you built.

511
00:44:52,065 --> 00:44:54,818
You should be the one tied and locked up.

512
00:44:55,485 --> 00:44:57,737
Regina isn't the crazy one here.

513
00:44:58,655 --> 00:44:59,739
It's you.

514
00:45:01,116 --> 00:45:02,951
Mara, don't ever come near--

515
00:45:11,751 --> 00:45:13,253
Hey, have you heard?

516
00:45:13,336 --> 00:45:14,838
Did you know
someone escaped again a while ago?

517
00:45:14,921 --> 00:45:17,257
Really? Who is it this time?

518
00:45:17,340 --> 00:45:21,177
It's patient Santos.
And she just got here.

519
00:46:00,425 --> 00:46:01,759
Ow!

520
00:46:02,343 --> 00:46:03,344
Sorry.

521
00:46:06,973 --> 00:46:08,141
Ana.

522
00:46:09,058 --> 00:46:11,311
You are extra spaced out today.

523
00:46:16,524 --> 00:46:19,027
Are you sure you're marrying Carlos?

524
00:46:21,905 --> 00:46:23,239
What?

525
00:46:24,282 --> 00:46:25,533
On the day of my wedding...

526
00:46:25,617 --> 00:46:27,702
you're going to say that, really?

527
00:46:28,703 --> 00:46:30,622
It just crossed my mind.

528
00:46:34,876 --> 00:46:37,629
I know Carlos and I
have been together for a long time.

529
00:46:37,712 --> 00:46:39,464
I even did a loyalty test on him...

530
00:46:39,547 --> 00:46:40,965
and he passed.

531
00:46:41,049 --> 00:46:42,091
So...

532
00:46:44,677 --> 00:46:47,096
If you don't want to do it, don't do it.

533
00:46:47,931 --> 00:46:49,599
Because once you commit...

534
00:46:50,475 --> 00:46:51,893
everything will change.

535
00:46:53,144 --> 00:46:56,147
Even the parts of you
that you're trying to protect.

536
00:46:58,066 --> 00:46:59,734
Ana, you're scaring me.

537
00:47:02,654 --> 00:47:04,739
That's the thing with marriages.

538
00:47:06,491 --> 00:47:09,577
Some yeses follow you
for the rest of your life.

539
00:47:18,127 --> 00:47:20,547
So are you going to do this or not?

540
00:47:23,216 --> 00:47:24,551
I'll do this.

541
00:47:25,176 --> 00:47:27,804
I think Carlos is worth taking the risk.

542
00:47:28,221 --> 00:47:29,806
Like Ben, right?

543
00:47:33,893 --> 00:47:35,395
Good for you.

544
00:47:37,230 --> 00:47:38,481
You're all set.

545
00:47:39,482 --> 00:47:40,650
You're all set.

546
00:47:48,491 --> 00:47:50,660
I'm just gonna go get changed.

547
00:48:58,478 --> 00:49:01,230
- Hello?
- <i>Sir, Regina escaped.</i>

548
00:49:01,314 --> 00:49:02,315
What?

549
00:49:02,398 --> 00:49:04,484
<i>Yes. She got out of the facility.</i>

550
00:49:05,943 --> 00:49:08,363
Sir, did you happen to see this woman?

551
00:49:08,446 --> 00:49:09,822
She's wearing a patient's uniform.

552
00:49:09,906 --> 00:49:11,741
I'm sorry. I haven't seen her.

553
00:49:12,825 --> 00:49:13,951
Thank you.

554
00:49:16,162 --> 00:49:17,246
Miss!

555
00:49:17,872 --> 00:49:20,625
Hello, did you happen to see this woman?

556
00:49:20,708 --> 00:49:22,835
She's wearing a patient's uniform.
Maybe she passed by here.

557
00:49:31,177 --> 00:49:34,180
- Sorry, but we haven't seen her.
- Thanks.

558
00:49:54,242 --> 00:49:56,077
- Ma'am, please stop!
- Don't touch me!

559
00:49:56,160 --> 00:49:58,079
- You'll get in trouble, ma'am!
- Ma'am, that's enough.

560
00:49:58,162 --> 00:50:00,748
What are you all looking at?
Stop staring at me!

561
00:50:00,832 --> 00:50:01,916
Ma'am, that's enough.

562
00:50:01,999 --> 00:50:03,584
Don't come near me,
or else I'll throw this at you!

563
00:50:03,668 --> 00:50:05,503
I was just looking around!

564
00:50:05,586 --> 00:50:07,505
Uh, mister?

565
00:50:09,132 --> 00:50:10,258
You can drop me off here.

566
00:50:13,886 --> 00:50:15,304
Security!

567
00:50:17,140 --> 00:50:18,766
Can I leave this with you for a moment?

568
00:50:18,850 --> 00:50:20,768
- Sure, ma'am.
- Thank you.

569
00:50:20,852 --> 00:50:22,270
I'll come back for it, I promise.

570
00:50:27,066 --> 00:50:28,860
There's a crazy person inside!

571
00:50:28,943 --> 00:50:31,112
- Don't touch me!
- She's throwing a tantrum.

572
00:50:31,195 --> 00:50:33,865
- Stay away from me!
- What's going on?

573
00:50:33,948 --> 00:50:35,032
There's a crazy person inside.

574
00:50:35,116 --> 00:50:36,909
Don't touch me! Let me go!

575
00:50:36,993 --> 00:50:38,703
- Regina!
- Ma'am, that's enough.

576
00:50:38,786 --> 00:50:40,455
- Stay away from me!
- Regina!

577
00:50:40,538 --> 00:50:43,291
- Ma'am.
- Thank God I found you. I'm here.

578
00:50:47,211 --> 00:50:49,797
You're a monster! You're a monster!

579
00:50:49,881 --> 00:50:51,466
You're a monster!

580
00:50:51,549 --> 00:50:54,218
- Regina, it's--
- Monster!

581
00:50:54,302 --> 00:50:55,636
A monster!

582
00:50:55,720 --> 00:50:57,930
- There's a monster! A monster!
- Regina!

583
00:50:58,014 --> 00:51:00,016
Regina! Wait!

584
00:51:00,600 --> 00:51:02,185
Okay. Thank you.

585
00:51:02,268 --> 00:51:05,646
Please call me right away
if she comes back.

586
00:51:08,024 --> 00:51:09,192
Thank you.

587
00:51:11,194 --> 00:51:12,904
Ging.

588
00:51:17,700 --> 00:51:19,619
- Regina!
- Leave me alone!

589
00:51:19,702 --> 00:51:21,370
- Wait!
- Go away!

590
00:51:21,454 --> 00:51:24,290
Regina! Please, wait!

591
00:51:31,047 --> 00:51:32,048
No! Go away!

592
00:51:32,131 --> 00:51:33,508
- Regina, stop!
- Stay away from me!

593
00:51:33,591 --> 00:51:35,843
- It's just me!
- Stay away from me!

594
00:51:35,927 --> 00:51:38,679
- Listen to me!
- Stay away from me!

595
00:51:38,763 --> 00:51:40,932
- Stay away from me!
- Please, listen to me!

596
00:51:41,015 --> 00:51:42,850
Ging...

597
00:51:44,977 --> 00:51:46,896
I don't want to!

598
00:51:51,359 --> 00:51:52,527
Mara!

599
00:51:53,694 --> 00:51:54,862
Fuck!

600
00:52:18,553 --> 00:52:20,304
Mara? Mara?

601
00:52:20,388 --> 00:52:22,557
Mara! Mara!

602
00:52:22,640 --> 00:52:24,058
This can't be happening!

603
00:52:24,141 --> 00:52:26,477
Mara!

604
00:52:26,561 --> 00:52:29,564
No, Mara!

605
00:52:29,647 --> 00:52:31,107
This can't be happening!

606
00:52:31,190 --> 00:52:34,193
Mara!

607
00:52:37,572 --> 00:52:40,741
Mara!

608
00:52:42,076 --> 00:52:44,579
This can't be happening!

609
00:52:48,958 --> 00:52:52,461
Mara!

610
00:52:53,421 --> 00:52:55,840
This can't be happening!

611
00:53:02,138 --> 00:53:04,557
Mara!

612
00:53:12,773 --> 00:53:14,609
This is all my fault...

613
00:53:14,692 --> 00:53:17,612
Ben, this is all my fault!

614
00:53:19,030 --> 00:53:21,032
This is all my fault!

615
00:53:33,878 --> 00:53:35,129

<i>Why does it matter</i>

616
00:53:35,212 --> 00:53:38,174
<i>what you think is real or not, Ana?</i>

617
00:53:38,257 --> 00:53:39,967
<i>Are you a client?</i>

618
00:53:40,468 --> 00:53:41,469
I am his wife.

619
00:53:41,552 --> 00:53:43,721


620
00:53:46,349 --> 00:53:48,643
There is something
you need to know about Ben.

621
00:53:50,269 --> 00:53:51,979
<i>We will conduct</i>
<i>a wide-scale search at sea.</i>

622
00:53:52,438 --> 00:53:54,106

<i>Sir, there are a lot of secrets here.</i>

623
00:53:54,190 --> 00:53:56,233
What about this yacht, what's its secret?

624
00:53:56,317 --> 00:53:59,695
Spotless, right? Only Attorney Ben
keeps his yacht this clean.

625
00:54:02,323 --> 00:54:03,991
We can't get in touch with Beth.

626
00:54:04,075 --> 00:54:06,535
Her flight wasn't canceled.

627
00:54:06,619 --> 00:54:09,121
Sir, another body was recovered.

628
00:54:09,205 --> 00:54:11,207
<i>I wonder</i>
<i>how many bodies were dumped out here?</i>

629
00:54:11,290 --> 00:54:12,792
<i>We're worried about Beth.</i>

630
00:54:12,875 --> 00:54:15,127
<i>We couldn't get a hold of her.</i>

631
00:54:17,213 --> 00:54:18,547
Is this about me?

632
00:54:19,256 --> 00:54:21,509
It's always about you, love.

633
00:54:21,592 --> 00:54:23,678
<i>Everything...</i>

634
00:54:24,220 --> 00:54:26,138
<i>is about you.</i>

635
00:54:28,432 --> 00:54:30,851

